    "title": "Securitize Stock Jumps After Hours As It Launches Tokenized Apple, Nvidia, Tesla Shares On Solana - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mohd Haider ,\n53 minutes ago Photo: Jirapong Manustrong / Shutterstock - ejk Securitize, Inc. (NYSE: SECZ ) shares are trending on Thursday night\nSecuritize Launches 12 Tokenized US Stocks On Solana Shares of the Miami-based tokenization company jumped 9.92% to $13.92 in after-hours trading on Thursday, following its announcement that it is bringing 12 major U.S. stocks onchain through a new product called \"Securitize Stocks.\"\nAccording to the company, Securitize has chosen Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) as the first network for launching Securitize Stocks, with transactions settled in USDC (CRYPTO: USDC) . The tokens are backed 1:1 by underlying shares and will trade on Securitize’s registered broker-dealer platform for eligible investors in the U.S., the EU and other permitted jurisdictions.\nThe initial lineup includes Apple Inc., Microsoft Corp., Nvidia Corp., Alphabet Inc., Tesla Inc., Meta Platforms Inc., Amazon.com Inc., Netflix Inc., Circle Internet Group Inc., Space Exploration Technologies Corp., Strategy Inc. and Palantir Technologies Inc .\nCarlos Domingo , Chairman and CEO of Securitize, said, \"Tokenized stocks should give investors more than a price on a wrapper that tracks a stock and is only offered offshore.\"\nTrading Metrics, Technical Analysis Securitize has a market capitalization of $2.07 billion, a 52-week high of $17.01 and a 52-week low of $5.14.\nThe Relative Strength Index (RSI) of SECZ stands at 54.58.\nThe stock has gained 16.79% over the past 12 months.\nSECZ is currently trading at 63.35% of its 52-week trading range.\nPrice Action: Shares closed on Thursday at $12.66, up 11.05%, according to Benzinga Pro data.\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\nPhoto: Jirapong Manustrong / Shutterstock",
    "summary": "53 minutes ago Photo: Jirapong Manustrong / Shutterstock - ejk Securitize, Inc. (NYSE: SECZ ) shares are trending on Thursday night Securitize Launches 12 Tokenized US Stocks On Solana Shares of the Miami-based tokenization company jumped 9.92% to $13.92 in after-hours trading on Thursday, following its announcement that it is bringing 12 major U.S. stocks onchain through a new product called \"Securitize Stocks.\" The tokens are backed 1:1 by underlying shares and will trade on Securitize’s registered broker-dealer platform for eligible investors in the U.S., the EU and other permitted jurisdictions.",
